<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>Swift to its close ebbs out life’s little day;</l><l>Earth’s joys grow dim, its glories pass away;</l><l>Change and decay in all around I see;</l><l>O Thou who changest not, abide with me.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>Come not in terrors, as the King of kings;</l><l>But kind and good, with healing in Thy wings:</l><l>Tears for all woes, a heart for every plea;</l><l>Come, Friend of sinners, thus abide with me.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>I need Thy presence every passing hour:</l><l>What but Thy grace can foil the tempter’s power?</l><l>Who like Thyself my guide and stay can be?</l><l>Through cloud and sunshine, oh, abide with me.</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>I fear no foe, with Thee at hand to bless:</l><l>Ills have no weight, and tears no bitterness:</l><l>Where is death’s sting? where, grave, thy victory?</l><l>I triumph still, if Thou abide with me.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
